.TH "REPROCTL\-LAUNCH" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-launch \- open a service or browser in the current worktree
context
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl launch\f[R] \f[I]service\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-worktree\f[R]
\f[I]branch\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open a service URL in the browser, or launch the capture Chrome
extension in a dedicated Playwright Chromium instance for transitional
manual preview.
.PP
For web services, the URL is resolved from \f[B]infra/services.json\f[R]
for the current worktree context and opened with \f[B]open\f[R](1).
Services with \f[B]launch.kind=url\f[R] and either
\f[B]portless_name\f[R] or \f[B]port\f[R] are launchable; services
without a browser URL remain start\-only.
.PP
For \f[B]capture\f[R], a pinned Playwright Chromium browser is launched
with \f[B]\-\-load\-extension\f[R] pointing at the worktree\(aqs
\f[B]apps/capture/dist/\f[R] directory.
A persistent per\-worktree user\-data\-dir is used at
\f[CR]/Users/gary/Projects/repro\-dev/repro/tmp/agent\-browser/profiles/<slug>/\f[R]
so browser state (cookies, DevTools settings) is preserved between
launches.
The workspace URL is also opened automatically in the same browser
instance.
Treat this as a transitional preview path, not the normative
extension\-verification workflow.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-worktree\f[R] \f[I]branch\f[R], \f[B]\-w\f[R] \f[I]branch\f[R]
Target a specific worktree instead of the current directory context.
.TP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\-\-help\f[R]
Show usage.
.SH SERVICES
The exact service list shown by \f[B]reproctl launch \-\-help\f[R] is
generated from \f[B]infra/services.json\f[R].
Today that includes \f[B]workspace\f[R], \f[B]api\-server\f[R],
\f[B]admin\f[R], \f[B]capture\f[R], \f[B]marketing\f[R], and
\f[B]storybook\-ui\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl launch workspace
Open the workspace in the default browser.
.TP
reproctl launch capture
Launch Chromium with the capture extension from the current worktree as
a transitional manual preview path.
.TP
reproctl launch capture \-\-worktree feat/my\-feature
Launch Chromium with the capture extension from a specific worktree as a
transitional manual preview path.
.TP
reproctl launch api\-server \-\-worktree feat/my\-feature
Open the API for a specific worktree.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]reproctl\f[R](1), \f[B]reproctl\-worktree\f[R](1)
